Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:45:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] tests: matmul row invariance (M 1..300, position,
 threads) + device_probe example

logis-center's [EMBED-BATCHED] dynamic mode on the CPU relies on each output row of a Linear
being a function of that input row only. matmul_m_invariance_tests measures it for the
embedding shapes (384->1152/384/3072, 1536->384) and the batched attention matmuls, with a
FNV digest to compare thread counts (CANDLE_MATMUL_INVARIANCE_DIGEST). CPU tests assert;
Metal / Vulkan variants are --ignored, report-only measurements.

device_probe prints `DEVICE_PROBE <backend> OK|FAIL` so CI can tell whether a hosted runner
can run GPU tests at all (virtualized macOS runners may have no Metal / MoltenVK device).

Measured (x86_64 AVX-512, 4 threads): M=2..300 rows bit-identical to M=300 in all shapes,
M=1 differs (gemm gemv path), reversed rows identical, digest identical for 1/2/3/4 threads.

